# Governed metadata UI

**ARCH-006** (runtime authority) · **ARCH-007** (kernel layers). Skill: `.agents/skills/metadata-eui-polish/`.

## Prime directive

Metadata declares intent. Runtime owns authority. Renderers paint; they do not fetch, authorize, or guess business rules.

## Import doors

- `@afenda/governed-surface` — shared types/builders/schemas
- `@afenda/governed-surface/server` — RSC sections
- `@afenda/governed-surface/client` — client islands
- `@afenda/governed-surface/metadata` — renderer dispatch only
- `@afenda/ui` must **not** import governed-surface

## Layer ownership (where to edit)

| Change | Layer |
| ------ | ----- |
| Global table chrome / KPI density | Profile + renderer |
| Module-specific row tone, columns, actions | Builder (+ runtime permission gate) |
| Contract shape | Schema (Zod) |
| Paint / cell formatting | Renderer |

Execution order: Runtime → Query → Builder → Resolver → Zod parse → Renderer → UI.

## List windows

- Metadata carries the **current server window** only (cursor, `pageSize`, `totalCount`, `hasNextPage`).
- Cursors are opaque; `@afenda/db` owns filter/sort/cursor application.
- Export and bulk work: server jobs or query tokens — never browser-side full-dataset loops.

## Renderer kernel rules

- One shipped renderer per id under `src/metadata/renderers/`.
- Respect `pnpm lint:governed-renderers` import allowlist on `renderers/**`.
- Invalid metadata must fail parse before render; safe production fallbacks only.

## Tests

`pnpm --filter @afenda/governed-surface test`, `pnpm lint:governed-renderers`, and `pnpm architecture:check` when changing registry, profiles, or docs links.
